# The engine tarball is `git archive` of everything tracked, and the desktop
# app is not the engine: somebody who downloads psi-slides.tar.gz to build
# slides should not find an Electron package in it that the README does not
# explain. The app ships as its own release assets on the same tag.
desktop/ export-ignore

# Finished plans, reviews and build diaries: the record of how a feature was
# decided, kept for contributors reading the history, not for someone building
# slides from the tarball.
docs/history/ export-ignore

# The same reasoning for the working documents at the top of the repository:
# the assistant brief, the build diary, the original specification, the open
# plans and to-do lists, and the changelog. Each is written for someone
# changing psi-slides and is partly a record of an earlier state; a reader of
# the tarball gets the README, the guides it links and the lectures. The
# release notes link the changelog at the tag, and the README links these
# files on GitHub. Anchored with a slash so a lecture folder cannot match.
/CLAUDE.md export-ignore
/HANDOFF.md export-ignore
/PRD.md export-ignore
/CHANGELOG.md export-ignore
/PLAN-*.md export-ignore
/TODO-*.md export-ignore
/docs/TODO-*.md export-ignore
